nt_1^2\\sech(8x)\\tanh(8x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{8}\\int_{8}^{16}\\sech u\\tanh u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{8}[-\\sech u]_{8}^{16} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{8}(\\sech 8-\\sech 16).\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[1,2]$, and the result is positive because $\\sech u$ decreases for $u>0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355ee97e-2d9d-513c-af30-19d7946e5740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490426} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf6b45f-ddee-5619-98e3-65ad83574b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\csch^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490443} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac28e6c-80dd-5da7-b9d8-4fcc754864fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5})\\sech (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490454} {:answer/id #uuid "b71279ad-1d95-5961-8910-c4a7b04f5a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490465} {:answer/id #uuid "f47af739-648c-5d6e-becf-e5d608136d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b71279ad-1d95-5961-8910-c4a7b04f5a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490465} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae38fbbc-5bf2-5219-ab70-662a16f02eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aec90261-3e41-5113-be2e-aad35ddf754d" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int\\sech^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{5x}{5}$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=1\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=1\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing the substitution and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\tanh u=\\sech^2 u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2(\\frac{5x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=1\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=1\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=1\\tanh(\\frac{5x}{5})+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030c3210-41d0-5d61-908e-6a5256cd4f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5})\\sech (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490413} {:answer/id #uuid "1a7625a0-da78-5b93-988d-411851e95bf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490416} {:answer/id #uuid "4e90ae45-661d-54de-a0ba-beeb24ace4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} {:answer/id #uuid "7f134b14-df14-5b6f-8f49-59aa902f5ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{6}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490444} {:answer/id #uuid "f313c669-3bcc-5d7a-8bcb-6c8ac49990b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}\\csch^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e90ae45-661d-54de-a0ba-beeb24ace4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce095602-03dd-5b07-943d-af6c81a7c8d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490471}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfb61a77-a546-509b-9714-acf060d2c17a" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int\\sech^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{6x}{5}$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing the substitution and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\tanh u=\\sech^2 u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2(\\frac{6x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh(\\frac{6x}{5})+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}]}
